{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781177072,"nonce":"XH3Ki8p6VRUsr5YHrl3SsdEWlLY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFI_PBA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/253","origin":"github"},"title":"Deployment 2026-06-11: line-following slew-limit (nav#66) + #250 carry-forwards","message":"## Purpose\n\nOn-water test of the **line-following cross-track slew-limiter** (the nav#66 first-cut fix) under the replan-churn conditions that caused the 2026-06-10 (#250) patch-test zig-zag, plus carry-forward verification of two #250 items.\n\n## Primary test — nav#66 cross-track slew-limiter (A/B)\n\nThe fix (rolker/unh_marine_navigation **PR #75**, `feature/issue-66`) adds a slew-limiter on the cross-track error fed to the `CrabbingPathFollower` PID, so a discontinuous reference step (planner replan / avoidance reshape moving the line) is ramped in instead of slamming the controller into the over-correction that drives the hunting. **Default 0.0 = disabled** — it must be enabled to test.\n\n**Pre-req — get the code on the boat.** PR #75 is not merged (default branch `jazzy`). Either merge #75 to `jazzy` after its Copilot review, or push `feature/issue-66` to gitcloud for a field build on gabby. Then rebuild `marine_nav_crabbing_path_follower`.\n\n**Enable / tune** (runtime, live-tunable):\n```\nros2 param list | grep slew          # confirm the exact name (likely FollowPath.cross_track_error_slew_rate on /bizzy/controller_server)\nros2 param set /bizzy/controller_server FollowPath.cross_track_error_slew_rate 3.0   # ~3.0 m/s start; 0.0 = off\n```\n~3.0 m/s sits above real lateral drift (~boat speed) and below an instantaneous replan step. If it works, set the value in `bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml` (cross-repo follow-up).\n\n**Procedure (A/B):**\n1. Run a survey line; once tracking, induce **replan churn** — a mid-line re-send / `override goto` / `replace_task` (this is what triggered the #250 zig-zag).\n2. With slew **off (0.0)**: expect the cross-track to step + yaw to spike + the boat to hunt.\n3. With slew **on (3.0)**: expect the step to ramp in and the helm to stay calm — clean line.\n4. Record a run bag for offline analysis (per-minute oscillation vs replan rate; reuse `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-06-10_issue250/zigzag_analyze.py`).\n\n**Watch:** `/bizzy/FollowPath/pid/pid_state.error` (the true cross-track error), `/bizzy/cmd_vel_nav.angular.z` (raw yaw), and `/bizzy/plan` (replan rate). Note: stable-reference lines already track clean at 3 kn (#250) — the test is specifically the *churned* case.\n\n**Watch-outs (from review):** the limiter throttles *any* large error rate, so re-acquisition from a big offset is also ramped in — don't set the rate too low (slows genuine recovery). A gap \u003e the PID reset threshold re-seeds and snaps.\n\n## Carry-forwards from #250\n\n- **`clear_grid` live verify** (rolker/cube_bathymetry#39, merged) — run a long enough M3 survey to grow the CUBE grid until the operator grid downlink stalls, then `ros2 service call /bizzy/sensors/m3/clear_grid std_srvs/srv/Trigger {}` and confirm the topside grid recovers. (Manual stopgap; durable tile-sync = unh_marine_autonomy#86.)\n- **Sidescan controls + auto-range retest** — the #31 \"controls in rqt over the bridge\" still won't actuate topside (root cause: `state`/`change_state` not in the udp_bridge sender config + rqt manual-refresh; durable fix = the generic control protocol, unh_marine_autonomy#140, not ready). For this trip just **characterize**: confirm boat-side control works, and capture the GCV auto-range behaviour for marine_tools#32 (report true range).\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- deadpool (dev) · gabby / mercat / salmon (as they come online)\n\n## Logs\n\n- (dev + per-host logs added at wrap-up)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}